      {
        "id": 11581,
        "name": "Chromium_Man",
        "username": "Chromium_Man",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/858c86/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-26T12:09:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I posted a few weeks ago about a laugher I had against Advanced Baron Blade, so it's only fair to post that Advanced Voss beat the snot out of me yesterday:</p><p><span>Advanced Voss vs. Haka, AZ, and Visionary in Megalopolis.</span></p><p>The game was uneventful until I ended up accidentally locking down Voss. &nbsp;Haka had Savage Mana out with every minion that had come out to that point under it. &nbsp;He also had the TCF Conquerer under Savage Mana thanks to Twist the Ether. &nbsp;Voss also had TtE on him, so I had him dealing Cold damage to AZ (highest HP) every turn and Visionary was at one HP, but in a Telekinetic Coccoon. &nbsp;Also, Rooftop Combat was in play and I was carefully avoiding doing more than 10 damage to Voss in a round to keep the environment in check while I ate every single target in Voss' deck. &nbsp;Then Voss turned the tables. &nbsp;</p><p>Haka was at about 5 HP and I thought all Voss had left in his deck was the TCF Stalwart and a bunch of Forced Deployments. &nbsp;I had left two Quark-Drive Translocators in play because I was confident the deck was minion free. &nbsp;At the start of Voss' turn (Sub-Zero Atmosphere was out) he played a Genebound Frost Hound that I had lost track of. &nbsp;Each QDT caused him to play another card: &nbsp;TCF Stalwart and Forced Deployment. &nbsp;Since it was still the start of turn, the GFH hit him for 2 and the Stalwart hit him for 3. &nbsp;Just enough damage to kill him, so every minion I had so painstakingly collected ends up in the trash seconds before Forced Deployment goes off. &nbsp;AND it's still the start of the turn, so they all get to act. &nbsp;AZ and Visionary managed to survive this ridiculous onslaught and AZ was even able to clear the board with a Fueled Freeze that I burned two hero ongoings for, but at this point there was no chance of surviving and Voss and his minions eventually overran the heroes. &nbsp;Sorry Megalopolis. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
